# READ-FIELD-CLOSURE (T7), the caller's nearest binding of a free name is its formal: callw (int: cnt) builds g by
# wrap(5) and calls g(); model's local S reads cnt, which model forwards.  callw(40) gives 40 -- not the root's 9, the
# unit's cell 11 or the copy made at callw's merge.  Exit 7; 81 otherwise.
int: cnt 7
fn: model (int: y) int
    S:
        int: v 0
        v: cnt
    S
    return: S\v
fn: wrap (int: k) fn: () int
    return: merge(y: k; model)
sub: poke ()
    node\cnt: 11
fn: callw (int: cnt) int
    @: g wrap(5)
    return: g()
cnt: 9
poke()
int: result callw(40)
int: ok 7
if: result != 40
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
